1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Clarice de' Medici (1493 - May 3, 1528) was the daughter of Piero di Lorenzo de' Medici and Alfonsina Orsini.
2 CONT
2 CONT Born in Florence, she was the granddaughter of Lorenzo de' Medici, niece of Pope Leo X and sister to Lorenzo II de' Medici. After her brother's premature death, she educated his daughter Catherine, the future Queen of France.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1508 she married to Filippo Strozzi the Younger and moved to Rome. Filippo and Clarice had ten children. The most notable were:
2 CONT
2 CONT *Piero Strozzi (about 1510 - 21 June 1558), condottiero and Marshal of France
2 CONT * Roberto Strozzi (died 1566), married Maddalena di Pierfrancesco de' Medici (Florence, c. 1523 - Rome, 14 April 1583), daughter of Pierfrancesco II de' Medici
2 CONT * Maria Strozzi, married Lorenzo Ridolfi
2 CONT * Leone Strozzi (15 October 1515 - 28 June 1554), condottiero and Knight of Malta
2 CONT * Giulio Strozzi (died 1537)
2 CONT * Vincenzo Strozzi (died Rome, c. 1537)
2 CONT * Alessandro Strozzi (died 1541)
2 CONT * Luigia Strozzi (died 1534), married Senator Luigi Capponi (patrician of Florence)
2 CONT * Maddalena Strozzi, married Count Flaminio dell'Anguillara
2 CONT * Lorenzo Strozzi (3 December 1513 - 14 December 1571), abbot and Cardinal
2 CONT
2 CONT From: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clarice_de%27_Medici
