2 CONT *'''Lorenzo II de Medici, Duca di Urbino (1)
2 CONT *'''M, #113660, b. 9 September 1492, d. 4 May 1519
2 CONT *Last Edited=4 Jun 2010
2 CONT *'''     Lorenzo II de Medici, Duca di Urbino was born on 9 September 1492. He was the son of Piero II de Medici and Alfonsina Orsini. He married Madeleine de la Tour, daughter of Jean III de la Tour, Comte d'Auvergne and Jeanne d
2 CONC e Bourbon, on 2 May 1518. A contract for the marriage of Lorenzo II de Medici, Duca di Urbino and Madeleine de la Tour was signed on 16 January 1517/18.3 He died on 4 May 1519 at age 26.
2 CONT *'''     He gained the title of Duca di Urbino.1 He held the office of Governor of Florence in 1513.4
2 CONT *'''Child of Lorenzo II de Medici, Duca di Urbino and Madeleine de la Tour
2 CONT **1. Catherine de Medici+ (1) b. 13 Apr 1519, d. 5 Jan 1589
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT * 1.[S16] Jirí Louda and Michael MacLagan, Lines of Succession: Heraldry of the Royal Families of Europe, 2nd edition (London, U.K.: Little, Brown and Company, 1999), table 67. Hereinafter cited as Lines of Succession.
2 CONT * 2.[S3409] Caroline Maubois, "re: Penancoet Family," e-mail message to Darryl Roger Lundy, 2 December 2008. Hereinafter cited as "re: Penancoet Family."
2 CONT * 3.[S6] G.E. Cokayne; with Vicary Gibbs, H.A. Doubleday, Geoffrey H. White, Duncan Warrand and Lord Howard de Walden, editors, The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain and the United Kingdom, Extant, Exti
2 CONC nct or Dormant, new ed., 13 volumes in 14 (1910-1959; reprint in 6 volumes, Gloucester, U.K.: Alan Sutton Publishing, 2000), volume I, page 82. Hereinafter cited as The Complete Peerage.
2 CONT * 4.[S38] John Morby, Dynasties of the World: a chronological and genealogical handbook (Oxford, Oxfordshire, U.K.: Oxford University Press, 1989), page 108. Hereinafter cited as Dynasties of the World.
2 CONT *From: http://thepeerage.com/p11366.htm#i113660
