1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Lucrezia de' Medici (14 February 1545 – 21 April 1561)[1] was the daughter of Cosimo I de' Medici and Eleanor of Toledo.
2 CONT
2 CONT Born in Florence, she was the first wife of Alfonso II d'Este, Duke of Modena and Ferrara, whom she married on 3 July 1558. She moved to Ferrara only two years later, after being abandoned by her husband, who preferred the court o
2 CONC f Henry II of France. Her sudden death spurred rumours that she was poisoned, but it is more likely that she instead died of tuberculosis.
2 CONT
2 CONT After the ground-breaking book of Louis S. Friedland of 1936, experts claim she is the Duchess on the painting referred to in Robert Browning's poem My Last Duchess.
