1 NOTE Louis XIV (1638-1715), king of France - the "Grand Monarch" - was the son of Louis XIII. His reign saw the French monarchy reach and pass its zenith. The bureaucratic machinery of central government was rearranged, and the monarch
2 CONC y became more absolute than ever. Then France became involved in a long series of wars. In 1700 the War of the Spanish Succession broke out, in which Louis fought to secure the crown of Spain for his grandson. Louis obtained wonde
2 CONC rfully favorable terms in the Peace of Utrecht (1713); but he had thrown away the internal prosperity of his country, and all share of the New World and chance of colonial empire. [World Wide Illustrated Encyclopedia, 1935]
1 NOTE Louis XIV of France became his 72-year reign as King of France in 1643, at first under the Regency of his mother, Anne of Austria, until 1651.  Louis XIV reigned until 1715, bringing about many of the changes, buildings, and re-st
2 CONC ructering of Paris which made it the show place of Europe.  He died in 1715, and was succeeded by  his nephew, Philip of Orleans.
