1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Charlotte Jemima Henrietta Maria FitzRoy (or Fitzcharles; 1650–1684) was the illegitimate daughter of Charles II of England and Elizabeth Killigrew[1], a Maid of Honour to Charles' mother, Henrietta Maria of France
2 CONC . Charlotte was a niece of Thomas Killigrew and stepdaughter of Francis Boyle, 1st Viscount Shannon.
2 CONT
2 CONT She married James Howard, a grandson of Theophilus Howard, 2nd Earl of Suffolk. In 1672 she married secondly William Paston, later the 2nd Earl of Yarmouth, a member of the gentry Paston family. Paston and his father, Robert Pasto
2 CONC n, 1st Earl of Yarmouth, were in high favour with the Stuarts.
2 CONT
2 CONT She died on 28 July 1684 and was interred at Westminster Abbey, London, England on 4 August 1684.
2 CONT
2 CONT >In 'King Charles II' by Antonia Fraser there's the picture of Charlotte Fitzroy (Lady Castlemaine's daughter) and it says she was Charles' favourite daughter.
2 CONT
2 CONT Links 
2 CONT * http://www.thepeerage.com/p10503.htm#i105026
2 CONT * http://forum.alexanderpalace.org/index.php?topic=3136.45
2 CONT
