1 NOTE BIOGRAPHY: 1st Duke of Richmond and Lennox
1 NOTE Richmond was a patron of cricket, then becoming a major professional sport, and did much to develop it in Sussex. It is almost certain that he was involved with the earliest known major cricket match which took place in the 1697 s
2 CONC eason and was the first to be reported by the press [1]. Richmond sponsored a team in the 1702 season against an Arundel side [2].
2 CONT
2 CONT Richmond's son Charles, the 2nd Duke, inherited his interest in cricket and became the patron of both Sussex county cricket teams and Slindon Cricket Club.
