1 NOTE {geni:about_me} III Duca della Mirandola, Principe del Sacro Romano Impero, V Marchese di Concordia, Signore di San Martino in Spino e Cividale. Ricevette nel 1691 l'Investitura Imperiale, fu dichiarato reo di fellonia dall"Impera
2 CONC tore nel 1704 e nel 1707 fu deposto. Nel 1708 subì la confisca dei beni e riparò in Spagna. Patrizio Veneto, Cavaliere del Tosone d'Oro 1724. Luogotenente Generale dell'Esercito Reale Francese 1704, Grande Scudiere del Re di Spagn
2 CONC a 1715, Maggiordono Maggiore del Re di Spagna 1717.
2 CONT
2 CONT ====Golden Fleece - Knights: Spanish Branch====
2 CONT * Wikipedia -  [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Francesco_Maria_Pico_della_Mirandola '''Francesco Maria Pico della Mirandola''']
2 CONT * https://www.treccani.it/enciclopedia/pico-francesco-maria-duca-della-mirandola_(Dizionario-Biografico)/
2 CONT Poiché entrambi i matrimoni erano rimasti sterili, con lui ebbe termine la linea diretta dei signori della Mirandola.  
2 CONT
2 CONT (His birth date is erroneously stated below as 1668)
2 CONT
2 CONT ====English====
2 CONT * Francesco Maria Pico della Mirandola (Mirandola September 20, 1668 - Madrid 1747) was the last Duke of Mirandola from 1691-1711. He was a son of Francesco Maria Pico della Mirandola and his wife Anna Camilla Borghese.
2 CONT * After his father died in 1689 he became Crown Prince of the Duchy. Two years later he succeeded his grandfather Alessandro II as duke. In 1711 he sold his duchy to [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rinaldo_d%27Este_%281655%E2%80%931
2 CONC 737%29 '''Rinaldo III d'Este'''], Duke of Modena.
2 CONT * Francesco Maria married twice. For the first time he married in 1716 in Madrid with Teresa Spinola y de la Cerda (26 april 1685 - Madrid September 15, 1723). At the age of 72 he joined on 11 October 1740 for the second time in m
2 CONC arriage with the 15-year-old Maria Guadalupe Fitzjames-Stuart y Colón de Portugal (Madrid, May 3, 1725 - there December 11, 1750), granddaughter of James FitzJames, Duke of Berwick and Liria y Xerica and thus granddaughter of [htt
2 CONC p://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/James_II_of_England '''King James II of England'''].
2 CONT * Both marriages were childless.
2 CONT ====Dutch====
2 CONT * Francesco Maria Pico della Mirandola (Mirandola 20 september 1668 – Madrid 1747) was de laatste '''hertog van Mirandola''' van 1691 tot 1711. 
2 CONT * Hij was een zoon van Francesco Maria Pico della Mirandola en diens vrouw Anna Camilla Borghese.
2 CONT * Nadat zijn vader in 1689 overleed werd hij erfprins van het hertogdom. Twee jaar later volgde hij zijn grootvader Alessandro II als hertog op. In 1711 verkocht hij zijn hertogdom aan Rinaldo III d'Este, hertog van Modena.
2 CONT * Francesco Maria huwde twee keer. Voor de eerste keer trouwde hij in 1716 te Madrid met Teresa Spinola y de la Cerda (26 april 1685 – Madrid 15 september 1723). 
2 CONT * Op 72-jarige leeftijd trad hij op 11 oktober 1740 voor de tweede maal in het huwelijk met de 15-jarige Maria Guadalupe Fitzjames-Stuart y Colón de Portugal (Madrid 3 mei 1725 – aldaar 11 december 1750), kleindochter van James Fi
2 CONC tzJames, hertog van Berwick en Liria y Xérica en daarmee achterkleindochter van [http://nl.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jacobus_II_van_Engeland '''koning Jacobus II van Engeland'''].
2 CONT * Beide huwelijken bleven kinderloos.
