1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * Voir [http://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Louis_Joseph_de_Guise '''Wikipedia...'''] Louis Joseph de Lorraine, Duc de Guise et Duc d'Angoulême, was the only son of Louis de Lorraine, Duc de Joyeuse, and his wife, Marie F
2 CONC rançoise de Valois, the only daughter of Louis-Emmanuel Louis-Emmanuel de Valois, Duc d'Angoulême, Count of Alès, Governor of Provence and granddaughter of Charles de Valois, Duc of Angoulême, an illegitimate of Charles IX of Fran
2 CONC ce. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was married on June 15, 1667, at Saint-Germain-en-Laye, to Élisabeth Marguerite d'Orléans, Duchesse d'Alençon, daughter of Gaston, Duke of Orléans, and his second wife, Marguerite of Lorraine, daughter of  Francis II, Duke of L
2 CONC orraine, and Countess Christina of Salm. 
2 CONT
2 CONT His body was interred at Joinville, the burial place of his ancestors, and his heart was buried at the abbey of Montmartre.* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/209344943/louis-joseph-de_lorraine,_duc_de_guise Find A G
2 CONC rave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Oct 11 2020, 15:41:10 UTC''
