1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Anne Lennard, Baroness Dacre=
2 CONT '''Anne Lennard, Baroness Dacre''' (17 August 1684-26 June 1755) was the daughter of Thomas Lennard, 1st and last Earl of Essex and Lady Anne Palmer.
2 CONT
2 CONT *She married, firstly, Richard Barrett, son of Dacre Barrett and Lady Jane Chichester, on 15 July 1716 at London, England.[1] 
2 CONT *She married, secondly, Henry Roper, 8th Baron Teynham, son of Christopher Roper, 5th Baron Teynham and Hon. Elizabeth Browne, in March 1717/18.[1] 
2 CONT *She married, thirdly, Hon. Robert Moore, son of Henry Hamilton-Moore, 3rd Earl of Drogheda and Mary Cole, on 16 October 1725 at London, England.[1] 
2 CONT *She died on 26 June 1755 at age 70.2
2 CONT
2 CONT * From 15 July 1716, her married name became Barrett-Lennard. 
2 CONT * She sold the Chevening estate, Kent for £28,000 in 1717 to James Stanhope, 1st Earl Stanhope.[2] 
2 CONT * From March 1717/18, her married name became Roper. 
2 CONT * From 16 October 1725, her married name became Moore. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She succeeded to the title of 16th Baroness Dacre [E., 1321] in 1741, suo jure, when the abeyance was terminated in her favour.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Child of Anne Lennard, Baroness Dacre and Hon. Robert Moore
2 CONT * Henry Moore [2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Child of Anne Lennard, Baroness Dacre and Richard Barrett
2 CONT * Thomas Barrett-Lennard, 17th Lord Dacre+[2] b. 20 Apr 1717, d. 12 Jan 1786
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Anne Lennard, Baroness Dacre and Henry Roper, 8th Baron Teynham
2 CONT * Hon. Anna Maria Roper+ b. 20 Aug 1719, d. 1782
2 CONT * Hon. Charles Roper+[2] b. 21 May 1721, d. 4 Feb 1754
2 CONT * Rev. Hon. Richard Henry Roper+ b. Nov 1723, d. Nov 1810
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT *1. [S37] Charles Mosley, editor, Burke's Peerage, Baronetage & Knightage, 107th edition, 3 volumes (Wilmington, Delaware, U.S.A.: Burke's Peerage (Genealogical Books) Ltd, 2003), volume 1, page 1181. Hereinafter cited as Burke's 
2 CONC Peerage and Baronetage, 107th edition.
2 CONT *2. [S37] Charles Mosley, Burke's Peerage and Baronetage, 107th edition, volume 1, page 1014.
2 CONT *[http://thepeerage.com/p2999.htm#i29984 From Darryl Lundy's Peerage page on Anne Lennard]
2 CONT *_____________
2 CONT *Anne Lennard, Countess of Sussex (25 February 1661-2 – 16 May 1721-2), formerly Lady Anne Palmer, alias Fitzroy, was the eldest daughter of Barbara Palmer née Villiers, 1st Duchess of Cleveland, and most likely Charles II of Engl
2 CONC and or Philip Stanhope, 2nd Earl of Chesterfield.  ....
2 CONT *Anne's husband the Earl of Sussex was a "popular but extravagant man"[5] who, by extravagance and losses by gambling, had to sell the estate of Herstmonceaux and others. Lord and Lady Sussex separated in 1688. She was widowed in 
2 CONC 1715.  ....
2 CONT *The children of her union with Sussex were two sons, who died in infancy; and two daughters, who lived to adulthood, co-heirs of the Barony Dacre:[6]
2 CONT **1.Barbara Lennard: born 12 July 1676 at Westminster, London; died 1741 at Paris. Married Charles Skelton, Esq., Lieutenant-General in the French service, and Grand Croix de St. Louis. Died without issue.
2 CONT **2.Charles Lennard: born 25 May 1682 at Windsor Castle; died 13 March 1684. Lord Dacre.
2 CONT **3.Henry Lennard: born about 1683 at Herstmonceaux, Sussex; died in infancy.
2 CONT **''''''4.Anne Lennard: born 17 August 1684 at Sussex; died 26 June 1755 at London. 16th Baroness Dacre in her own right. Married thrice;[7]
2 CONT **''''''(1) First, to Richard Barrett-Lennard, Esq. (died 1716), son of Dacre Barrett-Lennard and his wife Jane, eldest daughter of Arthur Chichester, the second Earl of Donegal. Died a few months after his marriage to the Lady An
2 CONC ne in 1716, leaving his wife with child. Their son was Thomas Barrett-Lennard, 17th Baron Dacre (1717 – 12 January 1786), who died without issue.
2 CONT **''''''(2) Secondly, to Henry Roper, 8th Baron Teynham (died 16 May 1723). Had, among other children, Charles, who m. Gertrude, sister and co-heir of John Trevor, esq. of Glynd, in Sussex, and left at his decease, in 1754,  ....
2 CONT **''''''(3) Thirdly, to Roger Moore, Esq., fifth son of Henry, Earl of Drogheda, in Ireland, by whom she had one son, Henry.
2 CONT *Her descendants include:
2 CONT *Alexander Murray, 8th Earl of Dunmore
2 CONT *Colonel Sir William Robert Campion
2 CONT *Thomas Coke, 3rd Earl of Leicester
2 CONT *William Legge, 7th Earl of Dartmouth
2 CONT *Gerald Legge, 9th Earl of Dartmouth
2 CONT *Lady Elizabeth Basset
2 CONT *Patrick Anson, 5th Earl of Lichfield
2 CONT *Nigel Forbes, 22nd Lord Forbes
2 CONT *Dermot Chichester, 7th Marquess of Donegall
2 CONT *Lavinia Fitzalan-Howard, Duchess of Norfolk
2 CONT *Richard Lyon-Dalberg-Acton, 4th Baron Acton
2 CONT *Reginald Manningham-Buller, 1st Viscount Dilhorne
2 CONT *Windham Wyndham-Quin, 5th Earl of Dunraven and Mount-Earl
2 CONT *Robert Gascoyne-Cecil, 7th Marquess of Salisbury
2 CONT *Max Wyndham, 2nd Baron Egremont
2 CONT *Sir Hugh Barrett-Lennard, 6th Baronet
2 CONT *Anne Lennard, Countess of Sussex should not be confused with her daughter, *Anne Barrett-Lennard, 16th Baroness Dacre.
2 CONT *The Countess of Sussex died May 16, 1721 or 1722, and was buried at Linsted, County Kent.
2 CONT
2 CONT *References
2 CONT *1.^ June Ferguson's Royalty GED
2 CONT *2.^ From Burnet's History of his Own Times, quoted in G. Steinman Steinman's A Memoir of Barbara, Duchess of Cleveland, 1871, page 26.
2 CONT *3.^ Cunningham and Goodwin's The Story of Nell Gwyn, 1903, page 196.
2 CONT *4.^ "Memoirs of the Court of England"
2 CONT *5.^ From John Heneage Jesse's Memoirs of the Court of England During the Reign of the Stuarts, 1855, page 170.
2 CONT *6.^ [1]
2 CONT *7.^ From Booker, von Alvensleben, W Owen's The Peerage of England, Scotland, and Ireland, 1790, pages 372-374.
2 CONT *[http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anne_Lennard,_Countess_of_Sussex Wiki]
