1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =='''Edmund Sheffield, 2nd Duke of Buckingham and Normanby, Marquess of Normanby'''==
2 CONT
2 CONT Edmund Sheffield, 2nd Duke of Buckingham and Normanby (11 January 1716 – 30 October 1735) was an English nobleman, styled Marquess of Normanby from 1716 to 1721.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT The legitimate son of John Sheffield, 1st Duke of Buckingham and Normanby, he succeeded his father in 1721. He matriculated at Queen's College, Oxford in 1732[2] and died of consumption in Rome in 1735. As he never married and lef
2 CONC t no issue, the dukedom became extinct upon his death. The family estates, including Normanby Park, devolved upon his illegitimate half brother Charles Herbert Sheffield.[3] 
2 CONT __________________________________________________________________
2 CONT Notes
2 CONT * Doyle, James William Edmund (1885). The Official Baronage of England, v. 1. London: Longmans, Green. p. 270. Retrieved 22 March 2009.
2 CONT * Foster, Joseph (1888–1892). "Sheffield, Edmund, (2nd) Duke of Buckingham" . Alumni Oxonienses: the Members of the University of Oxford, 1715–1886. Oxford: Parker and Co – via Wikisource.
2 CONT *Cokayne 1906, p. 102.
2 CONT
2 CONT References:
2 CONT Cokayne, George Edward, ed. (1906), Complete Baronetage 1707–1800, vol. 5, Exeter: William Pollard and Co, p. 102–103
2 CONT
2 CONT * "<em>[http://www.westminster-abbey.org/our-history/people/john-sheffield,-duke-of-buckingham John Sheffield, Duke of Buckingham]</em>", Westminster Abbey
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Edmund_Sheffield,_2nd_Duke_of_Buckingham_and_Normanby
