2 CONT Victor Amadeus III of Savoy
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT   (Redirected from Victor Amadeus III of Sardinia)
2 CONT
2 CONT Jump to: navigation, search
2 CONT
2 CONT Victor Amadeus III
2 CONT
2 CONT Duke of Savoy, Piedmont, and Aosta, King of Sardinia
2 CONT
2 CONT King of Sardinia
2 CONT
2 CONT Reign 	20 February 1773 – 16 October 1796
2 CONT
2 CONT Predecessor 	Charles Emmanuel III
2 CONT
2 CONT Successor 	Charles Emmanuel IV
2 CONT
2 CONT Spouse 	Maria Antonietta of Spain
2 CONT
2 CONT Issue
2 CONT
2 CONT Charles Emmanuel IV of Savoy
2 CONT
2 CONT Marie Joséphine, Countess of Provence
2 CONT
2 CONT Marie Thérèse
2 CONT
2 CONT Maria Ana, Duchess of Chablais
2 CONT
2 CONT Vittorio Emanuele I
2 CONT
2 CONT Maurizio Giuseppe Maria, Duke of Montferrat
2 CONT
2 CONT Maria Carolina, Electoral Princess of Saxony
2 CONT
2 CONT Carlo Felice I
2 CONT
2 CONT Giuseppe Benedetto, Count of Moriana and Asti
2 CONT
2 CONT Father 	Charles Emmanuel III of Savoy
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother 	Polyxena Christina of Hesse-Rotenburg
2 CONT
2 CONT Born 	26 June 1726(1726-06-26)
2 CONT
2 CONT Turin, Piedmont
2 CONT
2 CONT Died 	16 October 1796 (aged 70)
2 CONT
2 CONT Castle of Moncalieri
2 CONT
2 CONT Victor Amadeus III (Italian: Vittorio Amedeo III di Savoia) (June 26, 1726, Turin, Piedmont – October 16, 1796) was King of Sardinia from 1773 until his death.
2 CONT
2 CONT Contents
2 CONT
2 CONT [show]
2 CONT
