2 CONT
2 CONT     * 2 Marriage and issue
2 CONT
2 CONT     * 3 Ancestry
2 CONT
2 CONT     * 4 External links
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit] Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Victor Amadeus III of Savoy.
2 CONT
2 CONT Born in Turin, he was a son of Charles Emmanuel III of Savoy and his second wife Polyxena Christina of Hesse-Rotenburg.
2 CONT
2 CONT Having succeeded his father in 1773, he soon started works of improvements in the port of Nice, and had dams in the Arce and the road of the Côte built.
2 CONT
2 CONT During in the Napoleonic Wars, his troops were defeated by the French at the Battle of Millesimo (April 13, 1796). Victor Amadeus was therefore forced to sign the Treaty of Paris, by which he ceded the fortress of Cuneo, Ceva, Ale
2 CONC ssandria and Tortona to France, and allowed free passage of the latter's armies towards Italy. He was also compelled to cede Nice and Savoy.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was a private conservative and very religious person, who, as a young boy, stayed far from public life. His father felt him to be unsuitable to hold power. When he came to the throne in 1773 and worked on bureaucratic and milit
2 CONC ary aspects of the reign. He was suspicious of anything innovative. However, he did implement several public works as well as paying a great deal of attention to his administration and armed forces. He approved and set up two new 
2 CONC important cultural state institutions on the advice of the bourgeoisie and aristocracy alike, the Academy of Science and the Agricultural Society
2 CONT
2 CONT He died soon thereafter in the Castle of Moncalieri.
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit] Marriage and issue
2 CONT
2 CONT Maria Carolina of Savoy.
2 CONT
2 CONT Coat of Arms of Kings of Sardinia of House of Savoy after 1720.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Infanta Maria Antonietta of Spain (1729-1785), youngest daughter of Philip V of Spain and Elisabeth of Parma.
2 CONT
2 CONT They had twelve children including:
2 CONT
2 CONT    1. Carlo Emanuele IV (1751-1819), married Princess Clotilde of France
2 CONT
2 CONT    2. Marie Elizabeth Charlotte, (1752-1753)
2 CONT
2 CONT    3. Marie Josephine Louise 1753-1810, married Louis XVIII of France
2 CONT
2 CONT    4. Amedeus Alexander, Duke of Montferrat (1754-1755).
2 CONT
2 CONT    5. Marie Thérèse (1756-1805), married Charles X of France
2 CONT
2 CONT    6. Maria Anna Carlotta Gabriella (1757-1824), married her uncle Benedetto, Duke of Chablais (1741-1808), no issue.
2 CONT
2 CONT    7. Vittorio Emanuele I (1759-1824), married Maria Theresia of Austria-Este
2 CONT
2 CONT    8. Maria Christine Josephine (1760-1768)
2 CONT
2 CONT    9. Maurizio Giuseppe Maria, Duke of Montferrat, (1762-b.1799) unmarried.
2 CONT
2 CONT   10. Maria Carolina Antonietta Adelaide (1764-1782) married Anton, later king of Saxony.
2 CONT
2 CONT   11. Carlo Felice I (1765–1831), married Maria Christina of Naples and Sicily, daughter of Maria Carolina of Austria
2 CONT
2 CONT   12. Giuseppe Benedetto (1766-1802), Count of Moriana (-1796), and Asti (1796-1802) unmarried.
2 CONT
2 CONT This page was last modified on 24 July 2010 at 14:18.
