1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Overview=
2 CONT
2 CONT In the debates on the policy that led to the War of American Independence, Charles Lennox was a firm supporter of the colonists, and he initiated the debate in 1778 calling for the removal of the troops from America. The adjoining
2 CONC  towns of Richmond and Lenox in Massachusetts were named in his honor.
2 CONT
2 CONT He also advocated a policy of concession in Ireland, with reference to which he originated the phrase "a union of hearts" which long afterwards became famous when his use of it had been forgotten. 
2 CONT
2 CONT =Sources=
2 CONT
