1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Frederick_Keppel
2 CONT
2 CONT Frederick Keppel (19 January 1728 – 27 December 1777), styled The Honourable from birth, was a British clergyman.
2 CONT
2 CONT Background
2 CONT
2 CONT Keppel was the fifth and fourth surviving son of Willem van Keppel, 2nd Earl of Albemarle and his wife Lady Anne Lennox, daughter of Charles Lennox, 1st Duke of Richmond. His older brothers were George Keppel, 3rd Earl of Albemarl
2 CONC e, who had succeeded their father as earl, Augustus Keppel, 1st Viscount Keppel, an admiral, raised to the peerage in his own right and the politician and military commander Hon. William Keppel.
2 CONT
2 CONT Career
2 CONT
2 CONT After his graduation with a Doctor of Divinity, Keppel was appointed Canon of the Eleventh Stall at St George's Chapel, Windsor in 1754, acting as chaplain first to King George II of Great Britain and then to the latter's son King
2 CONC  George III of the United Kingdom. He was consecrated as Bishop of Exeter in 1762 and became Dean of Windsor as well as consequently Register of the Order of the Garter three years later, holding all three posts until his death in
2 CONC  1777.
2 CONT
2 CONT Family
2 CONT
2 CONT On 13 September 1758, he married Laura Walpole, sister of Maria, Duchess of Gloucester and Edinburgh and eldest daughter of Hon. Edward Walpole, a son of Robert Walpole, 1st Earl of Orford. They had four children, three daughters 
2 CONC and one son. Keppel died in 1777 and his wife survived him until 1813. His daughter Laura was wife of George FitzRoy, 2nd Baron Southampton. [
2 CONT
2 CONT https://ancestors.familysearch.org/en/M9X8-3NR/rt.-rev.-hon.-frederick-keppel-1728-1777
2 CONT https://prabook.com/web/frederick.keppel/2449538
2 CONT https://royalsandnobles.com/getperson.php?personID=P7012&tree=europe
2 CONT https://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Dictionary_of_National_Biography,_1885-1900/Keppel,_Frederick
2 CONT https://www.allabouthistory.co.uk/History/Low_Countries/Person/Frederick-Keppel-Bishop-of-Exeter-1729-1777.html
2 CONT https://familypedia.fandom.com/wiki/Frederick_Keppel_(1728-1777)
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/202062556/frederick-keppel
2 CONT
2 CONT Burial Date: 2 January 1778.
2 CONT Rt. Reverend and Honorable. s/o William and Anne Keppel, second earl of Albemarle. Educated at Westminster School and Christ Church, Oxford; MA, 1754; D.D. 1762; Chaplain in Ordinary to George II and George III; canon of Windsor 1
2 CONC 754-1762; Bishop of Exeter 1762; Dean of Windsor 1765. Registrar of the Garter 1765.
