2 CONT
2 CONT >On 14 June 1716, he [Francesco Maria Pico della Mirandola] married Duchess María Teresa Spínola y de la Cerda, daughter of Duke Carlos Felipe Antonio Spinola (fourth Duke of Sextus and Marquis of Los Balbases as well as Grande de
2 CONC  España), who drowned on 15 September 1723 during a flood that swept through their house in Madrid;[3] Francesco Pio di Savoia (Francisco Pío de Saboya y Moura) also died in the tragedy.[4] In 1744 he married in second marriage ''
2 CONC 'Maria Guadalupe Fitz-James Stuart y Colón de Portugal''' (1725-1750), daughter of James Fitz-James Stuart, 2nd Duke of Berwick and Catalina Ventura Colón de Portugal, 8th Duchess of Veragua. He died in Madrid in 1747, without son
2 CONC s.
2 CONT
