1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''William Roper''' was born on 7 January 1768 the son of Rev. Hon. Richard Henry Roper and Mary Tenison. He married Elizabeth Fish, daughter of R Fish. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was a Barrister and lived at Rathfarnham Castle, County Dublin, Ireland. He died on 16 July 1832 at age 64.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of William Roper and Elizabeth Fish
2 CONT * Charles Roper d. 9 May 1861
2 CONT * Jane Anne Roper d. 9 Feb 1849
2 CONT * Eliza Roper d. 18 Feb 1881
2 CONT * Isabella Roper d. 5 Apr 1876
2 CONT * Sir Henry Roper b. 16 Apr 1800, d. 20 Mar 1863
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations and Links:
2 CONT * http://www.thepeerage.com/p3546.htm#i35454 
2 CONT * http://www.stirnet.com/genie/data/british/qr/roper2.php 
2 CONT
2 CONT William Roper of Rathfarnham Castle (b 07.01.1768, d 16.07.1832) had issue  m. Elizabeh Fish (d 1845, dau of R. Fish) 
2 CONT
2 CONT *Blake, page 122. 
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1812, the family leased the estate to the Ropers and removed their valuable possessions to Loftus Hall in Wexford. The lands and castle were then used for dairy farming and fell into disrepair.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rathfarnham_Castle
