3 CITY London
3 STAE England
3 CTRY United Kingdom
1 DEAT
2 DATE 23 NOV 1831
2 ADDR
3 CITY London
3 STAE England
3 CTRY United Kingdom
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Member of Parliament.1 He was Joint Clerk of the Crown and Hanaper, King's Bench [Ireland].
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Family and Education b. 20 Dec. 1748, 3rd s. of Francis, 1st Earl of Hertford, and bro. of Francis, Visct. Beauchamp, and of Hon. George, Henry, Hugh, and William Seymour Conway.  educ. Eton 1760-5.  m. (1) 15 June 1773, Anne (d. 
2 CONC 29 Nov. 1804), da. of Peter Delmé, M.P., sis. of Peter Delmé, 1s. 4da.; (2) 2 May 1806, Anderlechtia Clarissa, da. of William, 4th Visct. Chetwynd [I], s.p.
2 CONT
2 CONT Offices Held
2 CONT
2 CONT Jt. clerk of the Crown King’s bench [I] 1790-1830, sole 1830- d.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ensign 40 Ft. 1766; lt. 2 Irish Horse 1766, capt. 8 Drag. 1770; maj. 3 Irish Horse 1773; lt. 3 Ft. Gds. and lt-col. 1775; served in America as a.d.c. to Gen. Clinton 1780-1; ret. 1782.
2 CONT
2 CONT Biography Seymour Conway’s behaviour in Parliament followed the family pattern: he supported North’s Administration, opposed Shelburne and supported the Coalition; and does not appear to have spoken in the House. His seat at Woott
2 CONC on Bassett was bought in 1784 from Henry St. John, who was managing the borough for his brother Lord Bolingbroke. He voted for Sir Elijah Impey’s impeachment, 9 May 1788, and against Pitt’s Regency proposals.
2 CONT
2 CONT He died 23 Nov. 1831.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ref Volumes: 1754-1790 Author: John Brooke Notes
