2 CONT '''Elizabeth Craven''' (née Lady Elizabeth Berkeley) (17 December 1750 – 13 January 1828), Princess Berkeley (though styled "Margravine of Brandenburg-Ansbach"), previously "Lady Craven" of Hamstead Marshall, was an author, playwr
2 CONC ight, traveller, and socialite, perhaps best known for her travelogues. She was the third child of the 4th Earl of Berkeley, born near Trafalgar Square in the English City of Westminster.
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Had many affairs, including with https://www.geni.com/people/Charles-Greville/6000000013019749375 after separating from her first husband in London.
2 CONT ----
