1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT https://www.digitale-sammlungen.de/en/view/bsb10006919?q=%28Edward+Petre%29&page=4,5
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Robert_Edward_Petre,_9th_Baron_Petre
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert Edward Petre, 9th Baron Petre (March 1742 Ingatestone Hall – 2 July 1801) was a British peer.
2 CONT
2 CONT Lord Petre was the son of Robert Petre, 8th Baron Petre (1713–1742), a renowned horticulturist, and Lady Henrietta Anna Mary Barbara Radclyffe (1714–1760), daughter of the 3rd Earl of Derwentwater (1689–1716) who was the grandson 
2 CONC of Charles II by his mistress Moll Davis.
2 CONT
2 CONT Lord Petre was a member of the English Roman Catholic nobility, a philanthropist and responsible for employing James Paine to design a new Thorndon Hall and a house in Mayfair.
2 CONT
2 CONT
