0 @N6000000002176641613@ NOTE He was the "illegitimate" son of Giuliano de' Medici. He, too, had an
1 CONT illegitimate son, fathered before the priesthood, Alessandro. Giulio was
1 CONT raised by his uncle Lorenzo the Magnificient. By the 1520s the descendants of
1 CONT Cosimo the Elder had become few in numbers. To insure that a Medici of the
1 CONT Cosimo line would continue to rule Florence, Giulio, then Pope Clement VII,
1 CONT installed his own illegitimate son as hereditary duke of Florence. That same
1 CONT year (1532) Clement VII abolished the city's old constitution.
