1 CONT
1 CONT Acceded 30 Jan 1649; Crowned in Scotland: Scone 1 Jan 1651; Restored 29 May
1 CONT 1660; Crowned in England: Westminster Abbey 23 Apr 1661.  His reign marked a
1 CONT periodof relative stabilty after the upheaval of the English Revolution. Noted
1 CONT for subservience and insistence on royal prerogative, his first Parliament was
1 CONT overwhelmingly Royalist and give him free rein.  Although a member of the
1 CONT Anglican church, Charles received the last rites of the Roman Catholic church.
1 CONT He was succeeded by his brother, James II.
